# CODEOWNERS — review routing and a map of the license frontier.
#
# This file does two jobs:
#   1. It routes pull-request review on the public GitHub repository
#      (olivaresai/olivares) to the people responsible for each subtree.
#   2. It documents the license frontier (LICENSING.md, REUSE.toml) at the
#      directory level, so a reviewer or an auditor can see at a glance which
#      tree is AGPL, which is Apache-2.0, and which is commercial.
#
# Honesty note (see GOVERNANCE.md): the project is beta and maintainer-led
# by a single maintainer today, so every path below resolves to the same owner.
# `@olivaresai/maintainers` is the GitHub team that must exist, with WRITE
# access, on the public repository for these rules to take effect (CODEOWNERS is a
# GitHub feature; owners without write access are ignored). As the
# contributor base grows, connector/SDK review can be delegated to additional
# owners here without touching the license frontier itself.
#
# Syntax: a path pattern followed by one or more owners (@user / @org/team).
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so the specific overrides below come after the
# catch-all. Reference: docs.github.com "About code owners".

# --- Catch-all -------------------------------------------------------------
*                               @olivaresai/maintainers

# --- AGPL-3.0-only: the product -------------------------------------------
/core/                          @olivaresai/maintainers
/modules/                       @olivaresai/maintainers
/web/                           @olivaresai/maintainers
/cmd/                           @olivaresai/maintainers
/operator/                      @olivaresai/maintainers
/terraform-provider-olivares/   @olivaresai/maintainers
/docs-site/                     @olivaresai/maintainers

# --- Apache-2.0: the permissive ecosystem boundary (the breadth moat) ------
# A connector must never import from /core (scripts/check-boundary.sh).
/sdk/                           @olivaresai/maintainers
/connectors/                    @olivaresai/maintainers

# NOTE: the commercial, additive Enterprise Edition (LicenseRef-Olivares-Commercial)
# is maintained in a separate, private repository — not in this public repo, and not
# a destination for community contributions (see GOVERNANCE.md).

# --- Licensing, governance & security: change with extra care --------------
# These define the legal and trust boundary of the project; route them to the
# maintainers explicitly even though the catch-all already would.
/LICENSE                        @olivaresai/maintainers
/LICENSES/                      @olivaresai/maintainers
/NOTICE                         @olivaresai/maintainers
/LICENSING.md                   @olivaresai/maintainers
/CLA.md                         @olivaresai/maintainers
/DCO                            @olivaresai/maintainers
/REUSE.toml                     @olivaresai/maintainers
/GOVERNANCE.md                  @olivaresai/maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md             @olivaresai/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                    @olivaresai/maintainers
/CHANGELOG.md                   @olivaresai/maintainers
/.github/                       @olivaresai/maintainers
/scripts/check-spdx.sh          @olivaresai/maintainers
/scripts/check-boundary.sh      @olivaresai/maintainers
